# Dev install after builds

On Windows, when a build of Lexiglance finishes and the user should try it on the desktop (the usual case after feature work), do **not** use the default `cmake --install` into `C:\Program Files (x86)\lexiglance`.

Use the project script so the build replaces the running install and restarts what was running:

```powershell
powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .github\scripts\dev-install.ps1 -Preset <build-dir-name> -SkipBuild
```

- `-Preset` matches the binary dir under `build/` (this machine’s usual tree is `win`, so `-Preset win`).
- Omit `-SkipBuild` only when you want the script to build that preset itself.
- The script stops `lexiglance` / `lexiglanced`, installs into `HKCU\Software\Lexiglance\InstallDir` or `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Lexiglance`, then restarts what was running.

Never treat a Program Files install as “done” when the user is running the AppData Programs copy.
